## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/h24/gb.png" alt="United Kingdom" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', marginRight: '8px'}} />United Kingdom

The United Kingdom faces its most serious US alliance crisis since Suez, with open diplomatic confrontation replacing managed accommodation as Trump employs economic coercion and attacks British military service. The bilateral web strategy through European partnerships appears increasingly necessary as constitutional actors including the Crown intervene in unprecedented ways. Domestic political fragmentation accelerates with continued Conservative defections to Reform UK and internal Labour tensions, while defensive economic measures attempt to navigate Trump's tariff regime.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** Trump threatened 10% baseline tariffs rising to 25% in June on UK and European allies over opposition to US control of Greenland. Starmer rejected the demands and condemned threats as 'completely wrong.' This represents escalation of Trump's economic coercion strategy targeting allies. *([The Guardian](https://theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/23/trump-news-at-a-glance-starmer), 2026-01-18)*
- **Diplomatic:** Trump claimed NATO troops 'stayed a little back, a little off the frontlines' in Afghanistan. Starmer responded that the remarks were 'insulting and frankly appalling' and suggested Trump should apologize for comments about 457 fallen British soldiers. This is unusually direct criticism of a US president by a UK PM. *([The Guardian](https://theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/23/trump-news-at-a-glance-starmer), 2026-01-23)*
- **Diplomatic:** King Charles allegedly raised concerns through private channels about Trump's claims regarding NATO troops in Afghanistan, reportedly contributing to Trump's subsequent backtrack. The monarch's intervention shows even constitutional actors being drawn into the diplomatic crisis. *([Daily Mail](https://dailymail.co.uk/news/article-15495331/Concerns-raised-King-Charles-prompted-Donald-Trump-Afghanistan.html), 2026-01-24)*
- **Domestic:** Labour's NEC voted 8-1 to block Greater Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham from standing in Gorton and Denton by-election. Decision fuels speculation about Burnham's leadership ambitions and deepens internal Labour tensions, with unions and MPs criticizing move as undemocratic. *([The Guardian](https://theguardian.com/politics/2026/jan/25/blocking-andy-burnham-keir-starmer-ruthlessness-weakness-labour), 2026-01-25)*
- **Domestic:** Shadow Justice Secretary Robert Jenrick and MP Andrew Rosindell defected to Reform UK within days. Badenoch sacked Jenrick before defection and warned against 'psychodrama.' Despite defections, polls show Badenoch's approval rating rising, suggesting some stabilization of Conservative position. *([The Guardian](https://theguardian.com/politics/2026/jan/19/kemi-badenoch-writes-tory-mps-party-on-right-despite-defections), 2026-01-25)*
- **Unexpected:** King Charles's direct intervention in US-UK diplomatic crisis.

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Starmer blocks Andy Burnham from Labour by-election amid leadership speculation** — Labour's National Executive Committee voted 8-1 to block Greater Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham from standing in the Gorton and Denton by-election, triggered by Andrew Gwynne's resignation. The decision fuels speculation about Burnham's leadership ambitions and deepens internal Labour tensions, with unions and MPs criticizing the move as undemocratic. *([theguardian.com](https://bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-01-25/starmer-rival-barred-from-contesting-seat-widening-labour-rift))*
- **NATO faces existential crisis over Trump's Greenland demands and alliance threats** — Trump's threats to impose tariffs on NATO allies over Greenland opposition and suggestions he might exit NATO sparked warnings of alliance collapse. NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte negotiated a 'framework deal' with Trump that defused immediate tensions, though details remain unclear. Eight European nations issued joint statement condemning Trump's approach. *([time.com](https://time.com/7353728/trump-nato-purpose-future-greenland))*
- **Former Bank of England analyst warns of financial crisis from alien disclosure** — Helen McCaw, former senior Bank of England analyst, wrote to Governor Andrew Bailey urging the central bank to prepare for potential financial market collapse if the US government confirms existence of alien life. McCaw warned of 'extreme price volatility' and called for contingency planning amid expectations of possible disclosure under Trump administration. *([gizmodo.com](https://independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/aliens-financial-crisis-bank-england-helen-mccaw-b2902690.html))*
- **MI5 and GCHQ assess security risks of Chinese mega-embassy approval** — MI5 Director General Sir Ken McCallum and GCHQ Director Anne Keast-Butler provided security assessment to ministers on approved Chinese 'super-embassy' in London. Security chiefs acknowledged risks cannot be eliminated but said mitigations are 'professional and proportionate,' while noting consolidating Chinese diplomats in one site has 'clear security advantages.' *([theguardian.com](https://theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/jan/20/chagos-donald-trump-keir-starmer-greenland-uk-politics-live))*
</Accordion>


